  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 153 AM MDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nHigh pressure has strengthened some more today, but on Sat a\nvery dry cold front is expected to move through Canada and\nMontana Sat afternoon/evening. During the prefrontal period, the\nincreased southerly flow should bring in hot air and\ntemperatures are expected to soar to record or near-record\nhighs. The air should be extremely dry and there will be an end\nto the spate of thunderstorms over the previous several days\nafter tonight. \n\nWind will be even stronger on Sun, but the cold air behind the\nfront will bring temperatures down into the 90s for most lower\nelevations on Sun. For Mon and Tue, high temperatures should be\nmainly in the 80s at lower elevations; however the low will have\ncontinued its eastward movement and wind should decrease.\n\nThe rest of the work week, Wed through Fri, look dry with a\nwarming trend returning to morning lows and afternoon highs,\nreaching the upper 90s by Thu or Fri. No precipitation is\nexpected during this time with the western states high shielding\ncentral and eastern Idaho from both remnants of the southwest\nmonsoon and cold fronts moving in from the north or west.",
